<title>USA: Maine Gov would weigh workers compensation reforms.</title>
<headline>Maine Gov would weigh workers compensation reforms.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine Gov. Angus King said he is willing to consider reforms to help injured workers, but would not support any major changes to the state's workers compensation laws.</p>
<p>King said the current system of representation of injured workers before the workers compensation board could be expanded and improved.</p>
<p>He said the pressure should be put on the board to improve the system. The governor says if that if the board does not, he will consider introducing legislation next January.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
